module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.type_alias_identity_decided_by_spelling_at_each_check

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { CeilingNotStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data type_alias_identity_decided_by_spelling_at_each_check: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "type_alias_identity_decided_by_spelling_at_each_check" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: CeilingNotStated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a type alias and its expansion are one type, yet each check that compares two types decided it separately. node_type_compatible compared spelled shape and took no symbol table; transparent_alias_identity_agrees was bolted on at individual call sites; the ExprIf join had none and refused an alias against its expansion. One-site patches in sequence: #13941 #14069 #13974 #14043 #14057, then #13939 added an Optional-specific identity leaf.",
    "HARM: a lawful program refused at whichever check lacked the fallback (surfaced by a private-repo PR after #13939 changed Present{} typing), and the fix at the prompting site left every sibling refusing. Roughly 35 alias-peel helpers in v1 inference and 30 in the Rust emitter each answered the same question.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the alias-and-expansion pair pushed through every check (if, match arm, argument, record field, return, list element, nested container element, function type; bare and applied; alias of a primitive and of a record) in dag/test/claim/alias_identity_every_check_witness.dag is the census. A name seam keyed on a bare string cannot settle an alias the consuming module never imported (ParseTree = Node read through another module's record field); the settled identity must come from the node's carried declaration.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable per site. CURRENT RUNG: mitigatable, one relation. The name seam (type_names_settle_to_one_declaration / bare_alias_settled_declaration / alias_head_reaches) is deleted; node and name entries (alias_settled_agree, alias_names_settled_agree) both reduce to settled_types_agree over settled_type, so Inner<IntAlias> settles identically at every site. Semantic change: the name relation now settles applied arguments where it used to stop at the head, and a bare name of a parameterized head refuses against an alias of an applied form. Executed evidence is NOT yet recorded here: dag/test/claim/alias_identity_every_check_witness.dag carries the alias-keyed argument-mismatch REDs (Inner<Int> vs Inner<Bool>) with accepted positive controls, pending a green run on the heal-converged head and the revert arm; the rung is not raised past mitigatable until then.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the capability is that every remaining expand_nominal_alias_rhs caller asks EXPANSION (structure of an alias right-hand side), identity having been routed through alias_identity_in_judgment / settled_declaration_of_type_name at the five sites 3757, 3781, 6174, 6210 and 5490 (#14330); and that infer carries a literal's inferred application, so the 05_emit_rust compensation type_node_carries_applicationless_parametric_head is deleted (its own follow-up PR, fixed at the infer producer, not the emitter).",
    "RETAINED SEAMS AND SCOPE (#14330): the claim is ONE SHARED RELATION FOR THE MIGRATED CALLERS, not for every comparison. Side-chat dispositions executed 2026-10-18: direct_call_structured_record_literal_resolved_type_mismatch now passes the original identity-bearing formal to application_type_names_compatible (no expansion-fed identity), and declared_alias_target_matches_produced (a spelling-keyed field-initializer fallback after node_type_compatible declined) is deleted with its call site; the nine alias_identity_every_check_witness controls and //gunbc/instruments:self-host stay green (exit 0, discriminating red established). Retained and named: expand_nominal_alias_rhs callers that ask expansion, and any site that a peel non-idempotence (v1_maintenance_standing) keeps from being unpeeled; each is an expansion caller by the per-caller table in the PR body.",
    "V2 RECEIPT, FIELD PROJECTION (2026-10-25, bold-koi-381, work item adhoc-b5f23a5d-052): the same class lived in v2.compiler.infer at ONE payload reader. infer_projection_receiver handed the receiver's established type to infer_projection_receiver_of_type raw, so for `h: Hash` with `type Hash = Fnv1a64Structural` the index answered the ALIAS declaration as the payload, an alias body declares no fields, and `h.digest` refused as infer_reason_field_not_declared_on_receiver: a correct program refused. Repaired by reading the receiver through infer_type_alias_normalized_at, the one alias rule the match scrutinee (infer_match_coproduct_of_type), the declared-type obligation, the generic formal match and the expected-type literal readers already use. SIBLING CENSUS (DESIGN 6b): of the infer sites that read a TYPE's declaration as a payload, the projection receiver was the only raw one; a construction names its declaration by tag reference and an alias-named construct refuses at assembly, a resolve-stage constructor-admission fact outside this census. Executed: v2.test.claim.compiler.lambda_alias_field_key, three arms FAIL on main and PASS with the repair (alias param, generic alias receiver, its instantiated-type discriminator) with five controls green on both; the reported lambda-key shape was already typed in v2 (the generic matcher normalizes before it binds) and is kept as the v2 control for the seed defect.",
    "SEMANTIC CHANGE, NOT OBSERVED (#14330, executed 2026-10-18): the name relation now settles applied arguments where the head-only relation stopped at the constructor. The intended discriminator, take(x: Inner { v: 1 }) against x: IntInner (= Inner<Int>), is ACCEPTED on both the regenerated mirrors and main's (witness read FAIL on both arms), so no probe built so far separates the two relations; the arg-mismatch REDs are refused on main too, by an independent check. The change is therefore a deletion of the head-only seam with no executed behavioral difference; if the settled-argument refusal of a bare parameterized name exists, its specimen is still unfound. Self-host and the nine witnesses pass on the new relation. NEXT TRIGGER: construct a probe where only the name relation decides (a bare parameterized name reaching application_type_names_compatible without a field-level refusal), or declare that none exists and delete the settled-argument branch from the name entry.",
    "SEED RECEIPT, GENERIC ELEMENT SLOT (2026-10-25, bold-koi-381 with smart-tern-402, work item adhoc-b5f23a5d-052): v1.compiler.infer unify_generic_child_pairs bound a callee type variable to the actual application's ELEMENT SLOT -- a node NAMED by the container declaration's own parameter (FreeMonoid's T) whose type lives only in its inferred -- instead of to that type, so every reader of the substitution keyed on the bound node's name or spelling saw an unbound T while its resolution was established. Two specimens, one link, both measured by an eprintln in the generated stage0 on main 88e8991e557: `fn(h) { h.digest }` keyed through a generic over `xs: List<Hash>` (`type Hash = Payload`) refused \"no field 'digest' on type 'T'\" because the field-access alias chain looks its next declaration up by that name (the sort_by wave hit it over v2.std.node `type Hash = Fnv1a64Structural` and worked around it with an annotated let); `skip(split(..), n: 1) |> first` left its Present arm undecided because a kernel-built List's slot is also SPELLED T (smart-tern-402, #15115). A record element escaped by accident, its slot's inferred being the record itself. Repaired at that link by generic_actual_position_type, which reads a leaf actual position through child_type_node (the read unify_callable_generics already applies to both sides); the formal stays raw for its own stated reason, and an application keeps its node because its inferred is its expansion. Census: the callable-parameter arm already read child_type_node and every other unify_generics caller passes a whole expression's resolved_type, so the child-pair arm was the one raw slot read; smart-tern-402's make_container_type spelling change was withdrawn with no measured remaining consumer. Executed: test.claim.generic_element_slot_binding_witness 7/7 PASS with the repair; on main exactly the two climbs FAIL and the five controls PASS. v2 control: v2.test.claim.compiler.lambda_alias_field_key lafk_a_lambda_key_through_an_imported_alias_types_its_field (v2 already types the shape; DESIGN section 7).",
  ],
  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_env", decl_name: "alias_settled_agree"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_types", decl_name: "alias_identity_in_judgment"),
  ],
}
